---Finds and replaces data in cells over a range, sheet, or all sheets.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.FindReplaceRequest
---@field find? string The value to search.
---@field matchCase? boolean True if the search is case sensitive.
---@field sheetId? number The sheet to find/replace over.
---@field matchEntireCell? boolean True if the find value should match the entire cell.
---@field allSheets? boolean True to find/replace over all sheets.
---@field range? gcp.sheets_v4.GridRange The range to find/replace over.
---@field replacement? string The value to use as the replacement.
---@field searchByRegex? boolean True if the find value is a regex. The regular expression and replacement should follow Java regex rules at https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/regex/Pattern.html. The replacement string is allowed to refer to capturing groups. For example, if one cell has the contents `"Google Sheets"` and another has `"Google Docs"`, then searching for `"o.* (.*)"` with a replacement of `"$1 Rocks"` would change the contents of the cells to `"GSheets Rocks"` and `"GDocs Rocks"` respectively.
---@field includeFormulas? boolean True if the search should include cells with formulas. False to skip cells with formulas.

---The result of the find/replace.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.FindReplaceResponse
---@field formulasChanged? number The number of formula cells changed.
---@field valuesChanged? number The number of non-formula cells changed.
---@field sheetsChanged? number The number of sheets changed.
---@field rowsChanged? number The number of rows changed.
---@field occurrencesChanged? number The number of occurrences (possibly multiple within a cell) changed. For example, if replacing `"e"` with `"o"` in `"Google Sheets"`, this would be `"3"` because `"Google Sheets"` -> `"Googlo Shoots"`.

---@class gcp.sheets_v4.GetByDataFilterSpreadsheetsRequest
---@field includeGridData? boolean True if grid data should be returned. This parameter is ignored if a field mask was set in the request.
---@field dataFilters? gcp.sheets_v4.DataFilterList The DataFilters used to select which ranges to retrieve from the spreadsheet.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetByDataFilterRequestCommentsViewModeEnum|string The comments view mode to apply to the spreadsheet. This allows viewing the spreadsheet with comments omitted or included. If one is not specified, COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED is used.
---@field excludeTablesInBandedRanges? boolean True if tables should be excluded in the banded ranges. False if not set.
---@field spreadsheetId string The spreadsheet to request.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetByDataFilterRequestCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsCommentsViewModeEnum "COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_DEFAULT_FOR_CURRENT_ACCESS"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED"|"COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED"

---@class gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsDeveloperMetadataRequest
---@field spreadsheetId string The ID of the spreadsheet to retrieve metadata from.
---@field metadataId number The ID of the developer metadata to retrieve.

---@class gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsRequest
---@field includeGridData? boolean True if grid data should be returned. This parameter is ignored if a field mask was set in the request.
---@field excludeTablesInBandedRanges? boolean True if tables should be excluded in the banded ranges. False if not set.
---@field ranges? gcp.sheets_v4.StringList The ranges to retrieve from the spreadsheet.
---@field commentsViewMode? gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsCommentsViewModeEnum|string The comments view mode to apply to the spreadsheet. This allows viewing the spreadsheet with comments omitted or included. If one is not specified, COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_OMITTED is used.
---@field spreadsheetId string The spreadsheet to request.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesDateTimeRenderOptionEnum "SERIAL_NUMBER"|"FORMATTED_STRING"

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesMajorDimensionEnum "DIMENSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"ROWS"|"COLUMNS"

---@class gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesRequest
---@field valueRenderOption? gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesValueRenderOptionEnum|string How values should be represented in the output. The default render option is FORMATTED_VALUE.
---@field spreadsheetId string The ID of the spreadsheet to retrieve data from.
---@field majorDimension? gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesMajorDimensionEnum|string The major dimension that results should use. For example, if the spreadsheet data in Sheet1 is: `A1=1,B1=2,A2=3,B2=4`, then requesting `range=Sheet1!A1:B2?majorDimension=ROWS` returns `[[1,2],[3,4]]`, whereas requesting `range=Sheet1!A1:B2?majorDimension=COLUMNS` returns `[[1,3],[2,4]]`.
---@field dateTimeRenderOption? gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesDateTimeRenderOptionEnum|string How dates, times, and durations should be represented in the output. This is ignored if value_render_option is FORMATTED_VALUE. The default dateTime render option is SERIAL_NUMBER.
---@field range string The [A1 notation or R1C1 notation](https://developers.google.com/workspace/sheets/api/guides/concepts#cell) of the range to retrieve values from.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.GetSpreadsheetsValuesValueRenderOptionEnum "FORMATTED_VALUE"|"UNFORMATTED_VALUE"|"FORMULA"

