---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotFilterSpecList gcp.sheets_v4.PivotFilterSpec[]

---A single grouping (either row or column) in a pivot table.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroup
---@field label? string The labels to use for the row/column groups which can be customized. For example, in the following pivot table, the row label is `Region` (which could be renamed to `State`) and the column label is `Product` (which could be renamed `Item`). Pivot tables created before December 2017 do not have header labels. If you'd like to add header labels to an existing pivot table, please delete the existing pivot table and then create a new pivot table with same parameters. +--------------+---------+-------+ | SUM of Units | Product | | | Region | Pen | Paper | +--------------+---------+-------+ | New York | 345 | 98 | | Oregon | 234 | 123 | | Tennessee | 531 | 415 | +--------------+---------+-------+ | Grand Total | 1110 | 636 | +--------------+---------+-------+
---@field sortOrder? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupSortOrderEnum|string The order the values in this group should be sorted.
---@field valueMetadata? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupValueMetadataList Metadata about values in the grouping.
---@field groupRule? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupRule The group rule to apply to this row/column group.
---@field repeatHeadings? boolean True if the headings in this pivot group should be repeated. This is only valid for row groupings and is ignored by columns. By default, we minimize repetition of headings by not showing higher level headings where they are the same. For example, even though the third row below corresponds to "Q1 Mar", "Q1" is not shown because it is redundant with previous rows. Setting repeat_headings to true would cause "Q1" to be repeated for "Feb" and "Mar". +--------------+ | Q1 | Jan | | | Feb | | | Mar | +--------+-----+ | Q1 Total | +--------------+
---@field showTotals? boolean True if the pivot table should include the totals for this grouping.
---@field valueBucket? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupSortValueBucket The bucket of the opposite pivot group to sort by. If not specified, sorting is alphabetical by this group's values.
---@field sourceColumnOffset? number The column offset of the source range that this grouping is based on. For example, if the source was `C10:E15`, a `sourceColumnOffset` of `0` means this group refers to column `C`, whereas the offset `1` would refer to column `D`.
---@field groupLimit? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupLimit The count limit on rows or columns to apply to this pivot group.
---@field dataSourceColumnReference? gcp.sheets_v4.DataSourceColumnReference The reference to the data source column this grouping is based on.

---The count limit on rows or columns in the pivot group.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupLimit
---@field countLimit? number The count limit.
---@field applyOrder? number The order in which the group limit is applied to the pivot table. Pivot group limits are applied from lower to higher order number. Order numbers are normalized to consecutive integers from 0. For write request, to fully customize the applying orders, all pivot group limits should have this field set with an unique number. Otherwise, the order is determined by the index in the PivotTable.rows list and then the PivotTable.columns list.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupList gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroup[]

---An optional setting on a PivotGroup that defines buckets for the values in the source data column rather than breaking out each individual value. Only one PivotGroup with a group rule may be added for each column in the source data, though on any given column you may add both a PivotGroup that has a rule and a PivotGroup that does not.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupRule
---@field dateTimeRule? gcp.sheets_v4.DateTimeRule A DateTimeRule.
---@field manualRule? gcp.sheets_v4.ManualRule A ManualRule.
---@field histogramRule? gcp.sheets_v4.HistogramRule A HistogramRule.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupSortOrderEnum "SORT_ORDER_UNSPECIFIED"|"ASCENDING"|"DESCENDING"

---Information about which values in a pivot group should be used for sorting.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupSortValueBucket
---@field buckets? gcp.sheets_v4.ExtendedValueList Determines the bucket from which values are chosen to sort. For example, in a pivot table with one row group & two column groups, the row group can list up to two values. The first value corresponds to a value within the first column group, and the second value corresponds to a value in the second column group. If no values are listed, this would indicate that the row should be sorted according to the "Grand Total" over the column groups. If a single value is listed, this would correspond to using the "Total" of that bucket.
---@field valuesIndex? number The offset in the PivotTable.values list which the values in this grouping should be sorted by.

---Metadata about a value in a pivot grouping.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupValueMetadata
---@field value? gcp.sheets_v4.ExtendedValue The calculated value the metadata corresponds to. (Note that formulaValue is not valid, because the values will be calculated.)
---@field collapsed? boolean True if the data corresponding to the value is collapsed.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupValueMetadataList gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupValueMetadata[]

---A pivot table.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotTable
---@field columns? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupList Each column grouping in the pivot table.
---@field filterSpecs? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotFilterSpecList The filters applied to the source columns before aggregating data for the pivot table. Both criteria and filter_specs are populated in responses. If both fields are specified in an update request, this field takes precedence.
---@field valueLayout? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotTableValueLayoutEnum|string Whether values should be listed horizontally (as columns) or vertically (as rows).
---@field values? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValueList A list of values to include in the pivot table.
---@field rows? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotGroupList Each row grouping in the pivot table.
---@field dataSourceId? string The ID of the data source the pivot table is reading data from.
---@field criteria? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotFilterCriteriaMap An optional mapping of filters per source column offset. The filters are applied before aggregating data into the pivot table. The map's key is the column offset of the source range that you want to filter, and the value is the criteria for that column. For example, if the source was `C10:E15`, a key of `0` will have the filter for column `C`, whereas the key `1` is for column `D`. This field is deprecated in favor of filter_specs.
---@field dataExecutionStatus? gcp.sheets_v4.DataExecutionStatus Output only. The data execution status for data source pivot tables.
---@field source? gcp.sheets_v4.GridRange The range the pivot table is reading data from.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotTableValueLayoutEnum "HORIZONTAL"|"VERTICAL"

---The definition of how a value in a pivot table should be calculated.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValue
---@field sourceColumnOffset? number The column offset of the source range that this value reads from. For example, if the source was `C10:E15`, a `sourceColumnOffset` of `0` means this value refers to column `C`, whereas the offset `1` would refer to column `D`.
---@field calculatedDisplayType? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValueCalculatedDisplayTypeEnum|string If specified, indicates that pivot values should be displayed as the result of a calculation with another pivot value. For example, if calculated_display_type is specified as PERCENT_OF_GRAND_TOTAL, all the pivot values are displayed as the percentage of the grand total. In the Sheets editor, this is referred to as "Show As" in the value section of a pivot table.
---@field dataSourceColumnReference? gcp.sheets_v4.DataSourceColumnReference The reference to the data source column that this value reads from.
---@field formula? string A custom formula to calculate the value. The formula must start with an `=` character.
---@field summarizeFunction? gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValueSummarizeFunctionEnum|string A function to summarize the value. If formula is set, the only supported values are SUM and CUSTOM. If sourceColumnOffset is set, then `CUSTOM` is not supported.
---@field name? string A name to use for the value.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValueCalculatedDisplayTypeEnum "PIVOT_VALUE_CALCULATED_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PERCENT_OF_ROW_TOTAL"|"PERCENT_OF_COLUMN_TOTAL"|"PERCENT_OF_GRAND_TOTAL"

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValueList gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValue[]

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PivotValueSummarizeFunctionEnum "PIVOT_STANDARD_VALUE_FUNCTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUM"|"COUNTA"|"COUNT"|"COUNTUNIQUE"|"AVERAGE"|"MAX"|"MIN"|"MEDIAN"|"PRODUCT"|"STDEV"|"STDEVP"|"VAR"|"VARP"|"CUSTOM"|"NONE"

---The style of a point on the chart.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PointStyle
---@field size? number The point size. If empty, a default size is used.
---@field shape? gcp.sheets_v4.PointStyleShapeEnum|string The point shape. If empty or unspecified, a default shape is used.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PointStyleShapeEnum "POINT_SHAPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CIRCLE"|"DIAMOND"|"HEXAGON"|"PENTAGON"|"SQUARE"|"STAR"|"TRIANGLE"|"X_MARK"

---Represents a single post in a comment thread.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.Post
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time the post was last updated.
---@field postId? string Output only. The unique ID of the post.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the post was created.
---@field assigneeEmail? string Optional. The email of the user who is being newly assigned to the thread as part of this post. Returns a 400 bad request error if: - The parent thread is a CommentThread whose headPost does not have an assignee. - commentAction is specified as `RESOLVE` or `REOPEN`. - `assignee_email` exceeds 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field commentAction? gcp.sheets_v4.PostCommentActionEnum|string Action taken as part of creating the post.
---@field deleted? boolean Output only. Whether the post is deleted. If `true`, content and author fields will be empty.
---@field author? gcp.sheets_v4.PostAuthor Output only. The user who created the post.
---@field fromImportedSpreadsheet? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from an imported spreadsheet. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field content? string The content of the post. Required to be non-empty if comment_action is not `RESOLVE` or `REOPEN`. This text content will be handled similarly to comments created in the Sheets editor. It will have similar behaviors for formatting, notifications, etc. May not exceed 2048 UTF-8 code units.
---@field fromCopiedSpreadsheet? boolean Output only. Whether the post is from a copied spreadsheet. This field cannot be set directly by callers.
---@field contentHtml? string Output only. The content of the post as HTML.

---Represents a user who authored a comment post.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.PostAuthor
---@field displayName? string The display name of the user. May be absent if the author is anonymous.
---@field user? string The resource name of the post author user, which can also be used to identify the user in the [Google People API](https://developers.google.com/people/api/rest/v1/people). Format: `users/{user}`. Will not be populated if the anonymous field is `true` or if the post is from an imported spreadsheet.
---@field me? boolean Whether the user is the authenticated user making the request.
---@field anonymous? boolean Whether the user is anonymous.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PostCommentActionEnum "COMMENT_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_COMMENT_ACTION_CHANGE"|"RESOLVE"|"REOPEN"

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.PostList gcp.sheets_v4.Post[]

---A protected range.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.ProtectedRange
---@field unprotectedRanges? gcp.sheets_v4.GridRangeList The list of unprotected ranges within a protected sheet. Unprotected ranges are only supported on protected sheets.
---@field description? string The description of this protected range.
---@field range? gcp.sheets_v4.GridRange The range that is being protected. The range may be fully unbounded, in which case this is considered a protected sheet. When writing, only one of range or named_range_id or table_id may be set.
---@field namedRangeId? string The named range this protected range is backed by, if any. When writing, only one of range or named_range_id or table_id may be set.
---@field tableId? string The table this protected range is backed by, if any. When writing, only one of range or named_range_id or table_id may be set.
---@field editors? gcp.sheets_v4.Editors The users and groups with edit access to the protected range. This field is only visible to users with edit access to the protected range and the document. Editors are not supported with warning_only protection.
---@field requestingUserCanEdit? boolean True if the user who requested this protected range can edit the protected area. This field is read-only.
---@field warningOnly? boolean True if this protected range will show a warning when editing. Warning-based protection means that every user can edit data in the protected range, except editing will prompt a warning asking the user to confirm the edit. When writing: if this field is true, then editors are ignored. Additionally, if this field is changed from true to false and the `editors` field is not set (nor included in the field mask), then the editors will be set to all the editors in the document.
---@field protectedRangeId? number The ID of the protected range. This field is read-only.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.ProtectedRangeList gcp.sheets_v4.ProtectedRange[]

---Randomizes the order of the rows in a range.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.RandomizeRangeRequest
---@field range? gcp.sheets_v4.GridRange The range to randomize.

---The status of a refresh cancellation. You can send a cancel request to explicitly cancel one or multiple data source object refreshes.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshCancellationStatus
---@field errorCode? gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshCancellationStatusErrorCodeEnum The error code.
---@field state? gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshCancellationStatusStateEnum The state of a call to cancel a refresh in Sheets.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshCancellationStatusErrorCodeEnum "REFRESH_CANCELLATION_ERROR_CODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXECUTION_NOT_FOUND"|"CANCEL_PERMISSION_DENIED"|"QUERY_EXECUTION_COMPLETED"|"CONCURRENT_CANCELLATION"|"CANCEL_OTHER_ERROR"

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshCancellationStatusStateEnum "REFRESH_CANCELLATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CANCEL_SUCCEEDED"|"CANCEL_FAILED"

---The execution status of refreshing one data source object.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshDataSourceObjectExecutionStatus
---@field dataExecutionStatus? gcp.sheets_v4.DataExecutionStatus The data execution status.
---@field reference? gcp.sheets_v4.DataSourceObjectReference Reference to a data source object being refreshed.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshDataSourceObjectExecutionStatusList gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshDataSourceObjectExecutionStatus[]

---Refreshes one or multiple data source objects in the spreadsheet by the specified references. The request requires an additional `bigquery.readonly` OAuth scope if you are refreshing a BigQuery data source. If there are multiple refresh requests referencing the same data source objects in one batch, only the last refresh request is processed, and all those requests will have the same response accordingly.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshDataSourceRequest
---@field isAll? boolean Refreshes all existing data source objects in the spreadsheet.
---@field dataSourceId? string Reference to a DataSource. If specified, refreshes all associated data source objects for the data source.
---@field references? gcp.sheets_v4.DataSourceObjectReferences References to data source objects to refresh.
---@field force? boolean Refreshes the data source objects regardless of the current state. If not set and a referenced data source object was in error state, the refresh will fail immediately.

---The response from refreshing one or multiple data source objects.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshDataSourceResponse
---@field statuses? gcp.sheets_v4.RefreshDataSourceObjectExecutionStatusList All the refresh status for the data source object references specified in the request. If is_all is specified, the field contains only those in failure status.

---Updates all cells in the range to the values in the given Cell object. Only the fields listed in the fields field are updated; others are unchanged. If writing a cell with a formula, the formula's ranges will automatically increment for each field in the range. For example, if writing a cell with formula `=A1` into range B2:C4, B2 would be `=A1`, B3 would be `=A2`, B4 would be `=A3`, C2 would be `=B1`, C3 would be `=B2`, C4 would be `=B3`. To keep the formula's ranges static, use the `$` indicator. For example, use the formula `=$A$1` to prevent both the row and the column from incrementing.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.RepeatCellRequest
---@field range? gcp.sheets_v4.GridRange The range to repeat the cell in.
---@field cell? gcp.sheets_v4.CellData The data to write.
---@field fields? string The fields that should be updated. At least one field must be specified. The root `cell` is implied and should not be specified. A single `"*"` can be used as short-hand for listing every field.

