---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.RowDataList gcp.sheets_v4.RowData[]

---A scorecard chart. Scorecard charts are used to highlight key performance indicators, known as KPIs, on the spreadsheet. A scorecard chart can represent things like total sales, average cost, or a top selling item. You can specify a single data value, or aggregate over a range of data. Percentage or absolute difference from a baseline value can be highlighted, like changes over time.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.ScorecardChartSpec
---@field keyValueFormat? gcp.sheets_v4.KeyValueFormat Formatting options for key value.
---@field customFormatOptions? gcp.sheets_v4.ChartCustomNumberFormatOptions Custom formatting options for numeric key/baseline values in scorecard chart. This field is used only when number_format_source is set to CUSTOM. This field is optional.
---@field numberFormatSource? gcp.sheets_v4.ScorecardChartSpecNumberFormatSourceEnum|string The number format source used in the scorecard chart. This field is optional.
---@field baselineValueFormat? gcp.sheets_v4.BaselineValueFormat Formatting options for baseline value. This field is needed only if baseline_value_data is specified.
---@field aggregateType? gcp.sheets_v4.ScorecardChartSpecAggregateTypeEnum|string The aggregation type for key and baseline chart data in scorecard chart. This field is not supported for data source charts. Use the ChartData.aggregateType field of the key_value_data or baseline_value_data instead for data source charts. This field is optional.
---@field keyValueData? gcp.sheets_v4.ChartData The data for scorecard key value.
---@field baselineValueData? gcp.sheets_v4.ChartData The data for scorecard baseline value. This field is optional.
---@field scaleFactor? number Value to scale scorecard key and baseline value. For example, a factor of 10 can be used to divide all values in the chart by 10. This field is optional.

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.ScorecardChartSpecAggregateTypeEnum "CHART_AGGREGATE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AVERAGE"|"COUNT"|"MAX"|"MEDIAN"|"MIN"|"SUM"

---@alias gcp.sheets_v4.ScorecardChartSpecNumberFormatSourceEnum "CHART_NUMBER_FORMAT_SOURCE_UNDEFINED"|"FROM_DATA"|"CUSTOM"

