---A sheet in a spreadsheet.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.Sheet
---@field protectedRanges? gcp.sheets_v4.ProtectedRangeList The protected ranges in this sheet.
---@field charts? gcp.sheets_v4.EmbeddedChartList The specifications of every chart on this sheet.
---@field columnGroups? gcp.sheets_v4.DimensionGroupList All column groups on this sheet, ordered by increasing range start index, then by group depth.
---@field filterViews? gcp.sheets_v4.FilterViewList The filter views in this sheet.
---@field data? gcp.sheets_v4.GridDataList Data in the grid, if this is a grid sheet. The number of GridData objects returned is dependent on the number of ranges requested on this sheet. For example, if this is representing `Sheet1`, and the spreadsheet was requested with ranges `Sheet1!A1:C10` and `Sheet1!D15:E20`, then the first GridData will have a startRow/startColumn of `0`, while the second one will have `startRow 14` (zero-based row 15), and `startColumn 3` (zero-based column D). For a DATA_SOURCE sheet, you can not request a specific range, the GridData contains all the values.
---@field tables? gcp.sheets_v4.TableList The tables on this sheet.
---@field rowGroups? gcp.sheets_v4.DimensionGroupList All row groups on this sheet, ordered by increasing range start index, then by group depth.
---@field slicers? gcp.sheets_v4.SlicerList The slicers on this sheet.
---@field conditionalFormats? gcp.sheets_v4.ConditionalFormatRuleList The conditional format rules in this sheet.
