---The table row properties.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.TableRowsProperties
---@field footerColorStyle? gcp.sheets_v4.ColorStyle The color of the last row. If this field is not set a footer is not added, the last row is filled with either first_band_color_style or second_band_color_style, depending on the color of the previous row. If updating an existing table without a footer to have a footer, the range will be expanded by 1 row. If updating an existing table with a footer and removing a footer, the range will be shrunk by 1 row.
---@field secondBandColorStyle? gcp.sheets_v4.ColorStyle The second color that is alternating. If this field is set, the second banded row is filled with the specified color. Otherwise, the second banded row is filled with a default color.
---@field firstBandColorStyle? gcp.sheets_v4.ColorStyle The first color that is alternating. If this field is set, the first banded row is filled with the specified color. Otherwise, the first banded row is filled with a default color.
---@field headerColorStyle? gcp.sheets_v4.ColorStyle The color of the header row. If this field is set, the header row is filled with the specified color. Otherwise, the header row is filled with a default color.

---The format of a run of text in a cell. Absent values indicate that the field isn't specified.
---@class gcp.sheets_v4.TextFormat
---@field foregroundColorStyle? gcp.sheets_v4.ColorStyle The foreground color of the text. If foreground_color is also set, this field takes precedence.
---@field strikethrough? boolean True if the text has a strikethrough.
---@field fontFamily? string The font family.
---@field underline? boolean True if the text is underlined.
---@field italic? boolean True if the text is italicized.
---@field link? gcp.sheets_v4.Link The link destination of the text, if any. Setting the link field in a TextFormatRun will clear the cell's existing links or a cell-level link set in the same request. When a link is set, the text foreground color will be set to the default link color and the text will be underlined. If these fields are modified in the same request, those values will be used instead of the link defaults.
---@field foregroundColor? gcp.sheets_v4.Color The foreground color of the text. Deprecated: Use foreground_color_style.
---@field bold? boolean True if the text is bold.
---@field fontSize? number The size of the font.

